Affirmation/negation pair on the SHARPENED RH rung: is the leaking banking order FORCED by the
functional equation, or free? Read the two ob3ects against each other.

Prior findings (2026-08-21), from the first pair (riemann off-line-arm lemma):
- Affirmation (confinement stated alone) = VACUOUS: crystal 3442270 (Collatz-descent), clean 12-word,
  cleared 0, final T. Presupposes the ⊙ fixed point; no clear fires; carries no information.
- Negation (a live off-line 2-orbit) = LEAKS: crystal 16402270 (two-fork-pair), over-wound 17-word,
  deposits 3 cleared 1, final Ftf (Belnap-both). The ≺ reflection clears the critical-line register
  with nothing banked behind it — the off-line orbit self-destructs.
- Repair: opening the ∈ hold-frame BEFORE the ≺ clear converts leak→banks (OK), final still Ftf on
  crystal 16402270. So the off-line orbit CAN bank as a both-valued object — its self-destruction was
  an artifact of banking ORDER, not the mathematics.

This pair settles whether that order is forced. If the affirmation (order forced, leak is the only
order) HOLDS/BANKS while the negation (order free, off-line zero banks) LEAKS/goes vacuous/F, the
functional equation forces confinement — RH's core. If the negation banks where the affirmation cannot,
the repair is available to a genuine zero and the off-line orbit coexists. If both go B, the order is a
genuine dialetheia — confinement is a choice of cork, not a forced collapse (the Collatz-cycle-on-L9 shape).

Register semantics: holds() = exposed empty AND live_clears>0; vacuous() = exposed empty AND
live_clears==0; leak = cleared with nothing banked; a count banked in an unfused frame is HELD.
The four-valued register (T closes, F ill-typed, N never forks, B both/barrier) is the holder opened
first and held through. banked's repair message names the fix: open the region that HOLDS the result
before the region that COMPUTES it.
